            <ArticleTitle>Strangulated appendix epiploica in paraumbilical hernia: preoperative diagnosis and laparoscopic treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Appendix epiploica can occasionally cause acute abdominal pain. The usual presentations are torsion or primary epiploic appendicitis. Strangulation inside a paraumbilical hernia with acute abdominal pain is seldom reported in the literature. The authors report a case of preoperative diagnosis and laparoscopic treatment of strangulated appendix epiploica in paraumbilical hernia that presented as acute abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
